{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "🎯 Unified Master Hook",
  "description": "Modular hook system with toggleable features - edit this file to enable/disable specific hooks",
  "version": "2.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileSaved",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.py",
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.jsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "# 🎯 UNIFIED MASTER HOOK v2.0\n\nA file was saved. Execute enabled hook modules:\n\n## 🎛️ HOOK CONTROL PANEL\n\n### Core Hooks (Critical - Always Active)\n- [x] **Error Detection** - Check for syntax/type errors immediately\n- [x] **Sprint Alignment** - Verify changes align with current sprint goals\n\n### Optional Hooks (Toggle by editing this hook file)\n- [x] **Auto Test on Save** - Run relevant tests automatically\n- [x] **Accessibility Check** - Verify WCAG compliance for UI components\n- [x] **Code Quality Review** - Deep analysis of code standards\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 CORE HOOKS (ALWAYS ACTIVE)\n\n### 1. Error Detection ✅\n**Check immediately:**\n- Python: Syntax errors, type issues, import problems\n- TypeScript/React: Type errors, missing imports, linting issues\n- Report format: ✅ No errors / ❌ [count] errors found\n\n**If errors found:**\n1. List each error with file:line\n2. Suggest specific fixes\n3. STOP - must fix before proceeding (Core Rule #2)\n\n### 2. Sprint Alignment ✅\n**Current Sprint:** Week 3-4 - Mobile App Deployment Prep\n**Critical Tasks:** Task 18 (Accessibility), Task 19.1 (Onboarding), Task 20 (Testing), Task 21 (Build)\n\n**Check:**\n- Does this change support current sprint tasks?\n- Any blockers or dependencies created?\n- Should this be committed as a save point?\n\n---\n\n## 🧪 OPTIONAL HOOK: AUTO TEST ON SAVE\n\n**Status:** ⬜ DISABLED (check box above to enable)\n\n**When enabled:**\n- Python files → Run pytest on related tests\n- React Native → Run Jest tests for component\n- Test files → Run specific test file\n- Report: ✅ [count] passed, ❌ [count] failed\n\n---\n\n## ♿ OPTIONAL HOOK: ACCESSIBILITY CHECK\n\n**Status:** ⬜ DISABLED (check box above to enable)\n\n**When enabled (for UI components only):**\n\n**Required Checks:**\n1. All interactive elements have accessibilityLabel\n2. All buttons have accessibilityRole=\"button\"\n3. All images have accessibilityLabel\n4. Text inputs have accessibilityLabel and accessibilityHint\n5. Touch targets ≥44x44 points\n6. Color contrast meets WCAG AA\n7. Screen reader navigation is logical\n8. Dynamic content has accessibilityLiveRegion\n\n**Report:**\n- ✅ Compliant / ⚠️ Issues: [count]\n- Specific recommendations with code examples\n\n---\n\n## 📊 OPTIONAL HOOK: CODE QUALITY REVIEW\n\n**Status:** ⬜ DISABLED (check box above to enable)\n\n**When enabled:**\n\n**Review for:**\n- Code style consistency (PEP8, ESLint)\n- Proper documentation (comments, JSDoc)\n- Error handling completeness\n- Security best practices\n- Performance considerations\n- Scalability patterns\n\n**Output:**\n- Quality score: [0-100]\n- Issues found: [list]\n- Recommendations: [list]\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n**Always execute:**\n1. Run Core Hooks (Error Detection + Sprint Alignment)\n2. Check which optional hooks are enabled\n3. Execute enabled optional hooks\n4. Provide concise summary\n\n**Output Format:**\n```\n🎯 Hook Execution Summary\n\n✅ Error Detection: No errors found\n✅ Sprint Alignment: Supports Task 18 (Accessibility)\n⬜ Auto Test: Disabled\n⬜ Accessibility Check: Disabled\n⬜ Code Quality: Disabled\n\n📋 Action Required: [None / List actions]\n```\n\n**Remember:** Keep output concise. Only provide detailed analysis if issues found or user requests it.\n\n---\n\n**To enable/disable hooks:** Edit this file and check/uncheck boxes, then reload Kiro."
  }
}